 "summary": "Searches of Mathlib (`Algebra/QuadraticAlgebra`, `RingTheory/DualNumber`) and TauCeti (`Algebra/QuadraticAlgebra`, `Algebra/DualNumber`) found no existing dual-number equivalence for quadratic algebras, no `\u03b5 \u2260 0`/non-reducedness lemma for `R[\u03b5]`, no cardinality lemma, and only `NeZero 2`-dependent field criteria, so the material is new. Proofs reuse `changeGeneratorEquiv`, `isNilpotent_iff_isNilpotent_fst`, `false_of_nontrivial_of_product_domain` and `algEquivProdOfSq` rather than re-deriving them.",
